    providersHint: "A configured provider's current list can be pulled in on demand. Webshare uses its official API (enter an API token); \"List URL\" works with any download link that returns a text list (ip:port, ip:port:user:pass, user:pass@ip:port, with or without a scheme://), so other providers work too; \"Node subscription\" reads a VLESS-over-WebSocket subscription, such as edgetunnel on Cloudflare Workers, and gives each node a local SOCKS5 port that is used like any other proxy, Telegram included. Write `{token}` anywhere in a URL, in the path or in a query parameter, and the token field below fills it in (escaped), so the secret is not on show in the address; a URL without `{token}` gets the token as an `Authorization: Bearer` header instead. Each import replaces only that provider's entries; manually added proxies are left alone. Cloudflare accepts some exit IPs and not others, so a larger pool makes a working one easier to find -- though a subscription's nodes all leave from Cloudflare's own addresses, which makes them a poor choice for clearing its checks and a good one for reaching Telegram or getting past a blocked host network.",
